<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     FAQ
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label fade-up">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="section-h2 fade-up delay-1">Common Questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list fade-up delay-1">

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">Will this disrupt my business?</button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. Our scan is entirely passive — it listens and observes traffic on your network without sending any requests that would interrupt service. Your team keeps working normally throughout the 15–30 minutes we're on site.</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">Do you install anything on our computers?</button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">No. We bring our own scanning equipment. Nothing is installed on your computers, servers, or network devices. We connect to your WiFi, run our scan, and take everything with us when we leave.</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">What if you find a serious problem?</button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">We explain it in plain English, walk through your options, and give you a clear priority order. No action is ever taken without your explicit approval. Many findings can be resolved by your existing IT provider using our report as a guide.</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">What do we actually get?</button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You get a clear report before we leave — every finding in plain English, a severity rating (Critical / Medium / Low), recommended next steps, and an executive summary you can share with your team or board.</div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
